  "test": "published-artifacts-and-permanent-cluster-wide-argocd-chart",
  "note": "Checks run after actual crates.io, GitHub and GHCR publication. Public assets and both Cargo archives match the reviewed exact-tag bytes. The globally installed Cargo CLI verifies automatic official catalog fetching before an isolated configuration refusal, with no Kubernetes endpoint or resource changes. The permanent four-node mixed-architecture installation changes from the tested candidate to the public 0.6.0 Helm chart through Argo CD, using built-in digest pins without component overrides. The original installation, registry PVC/volume, nine credential identities and bytes, administrator policy, and 203 prior release UIDs/specifications remain unchanged. Complete authenticated OCI graph readback verifies 18 prior and 35 new graphs. Historical metadata from retired backends is not claimed as verified registry bytes. Native frozen-input execution, fresh placement/cache/refusal cases and later ARM64 demand after base recreation were completed before publication with the byte-identical component catalog and chart, as recorded separately; they are not relabeled as published-artifact tests. This permanent-install verification does not uninstall, downgrade, interrupt controllers or change shared Nodes. Initial live-site hashes precede the publication-receipt documentation update. Private node names, kubeconfig context, credential material and infrastructure repository details are omitted.",
